ted along the Intracoastal Waterway in Little River on more than 115 acres of forest and marshland. This facility includes approximately 3 miles of nature trails and boardwalks that meander through its botanical gardens and along its waterfront. A small segment of the original Kings Highway, a colonial route between Boston and Charleston, still remains at the front of the property, behind the CB Berry Community Center. Beach Wheelchairs available by reservation for Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens. Call 843-381-8000 Monday through Friday 8 am – 5 pm or send an email to PGEgaHJlZj0ibWFpbHRvOmJlYWNod2hlZWxjaGFpckBob3JyeWNvdW50eS5vcmciPmJlYWNod2hlZWxjaGFpckBob3JyeWNvdW50eS5vcmc8L2E+ to reserve at least two days in advance. Socastee Recreational Park is located on a 91.5 acre property off of Enterprise Road and serves residents living in the southern end of the county. The facility boasts numerous multi-purpose fields, picnic areas, a disc-golf course, trails, and a playground. County Parks Vereen Memorial Gardens and CB Community Center 843-249-4157 2250 Hwy 179, Little River 29566 Monday - Friday (8 am - 5 pm) Saturday & Sunday (Closed) Located along the Intracoastal Waterway in Little River on more than 115 acres of forest and marshland, this facility includes approximately 3 miles of nature trails and boardwalks that meander through its botanical gardens and along its waterfront. A small segment of the original Kings Highway, a colonial route between Boston and Charleston, still remains on the property, behind the CB Berry Community Center. The Center provides space for recreational programming and community events. Like Us On Facebook Carolina Forest Recreation Center (843) 915-5332 Location: 2250 Carolina Forest Blvd, Myrtle Beach 29579 Monday - Thursday (8 am - 8 pm) Friday (8 am - 6 pm) Saturday (8 am - 12 pm) Sunday (Closed) Like Us On Facebook James Frazier Community Center (843) 397-1018 Location: 1370 Bucksport Rd, Conway 29527 Monday - Friday (8 am - 8 pm