litary Appreciation Days National Flood Insurance Program Parking Meters Resident Parking Decals SC's Largest Garage Sale Special Events Starting or Relocating a Business Tents, Umbrellas & Shading Devices Victim Advocate Office Wall of Service Pay Parking Meter Ticket Traffic/Criminal Ticket Utility Bill Report Code Violations Request for Rezoning Service Requests Watch City Council Online Careers Apply Online (Jobs) Employee Benefits Human Resources Employee Portal Services Bicycle Map & Routes Bids & Procurement Chair/Umbrella Rentals & Accessibility Code Enforcement & Quality of Life Court Flood Protection Friday Fax Memo Hurricane Preparedness Opioid Response Program Parking Meters Pay My Bill Pay My Bill Police-to-Citizen (P2C) Reports Receive Emergency Alerts Resident Parking Decal Program Special Events Service Requests Solid Waste & Recycling Special Events Surplus Auction Items Utility Billing & Service Departments Business License Division Capital Projects Department City Attorney's Office City Manager's Office City of Myrtle Beach Municipal Court Construction Services Department Community Engagement Office Communications and Creative Services Department Economic Development Office Emergency Management Division Financial Management & Reporting Financial Services Department Fire Department GIS Division Human Resources Department Insurance & Risk Services Myrtle Beach Convention Center Neighborhood Services Department Opioid Response Program Parks, Recreation & Sports Tourism Department Planning & Zoning Department Police Department Public Works Department Procurement Division Solid Waste & Recycling Division Sports Tourism Division Utility Billing Division Victim Advocate Division Government Boards, Commissions & Committees City Attorney's Office City Manager's Office Form of Government Friday Fax Memo Mayor & City Council Meeting Schedule & Agendas Polling Places & Elections Visitors About Myrtle Beach Beach Conditions & Laws Beach Water Quality Bicycle Maps & Routes City Events List Conventions Golf Cart Laws Host a Special Event Rent a Facility SC's Largest Garage Sale Tents & Umbrellas Military Appreciation Days Vacation Information Go Home More News Don't forget Myrtle Beach's six decal and placard options for parking season Don't forget Myrtle Beach's six decal and placard options for parking season FEBRUARY 28, 2023 The paid parking season begins tomorrow, Wednesday, March 1, in Myrtle Beach. Outside of paying the meter to park, there are six parking pass, decal and placard options depending on whether you live in Myrtle Beach or not. See the options below, and click the link for the full details and explanation of each pass, decal and placard option: https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/.../parking.../index.php . Remember, just because your home address says "Myrtle Beach," it does not mean you live within the city limits. You can check to see if you live inside the City of Myrtle Beach here: https://bit.ly/3Skao5y . Minor details for available parking options are as follows... 1. Resident Parking Decal - Free with proof of City of Myrtle Beach residency and paid vehicle tax. - Your vehicle must "live" in the City of Myrtle Beach limits. 2. Guest Placard - For residential properties east of Kings Highway, 31st Avenue North to 82nd Avenue North. - Four placards per address limit (no fee) 3. Seven Day Visitor Parking Pass for Metered Parking - Cost is $50.00. - Passes cannot be used in decal-only restricted parking. - Passes are available from Reef Parking in the Pavilion Parking Garage, 914 North Kings Highway, (843-626-7275). 4. Non-Resident Employee Decal - Must be directly employed by a business located East of Kings Highway to the oceanfront. - $50 per calendar year 5. Non-Resident Decal/Placard - Placards can be used at designated metered parking, located between 6th Avenue South and 21st Avenue North, and at metered street ends, from 69th to 77th Avenues North (not to be used in decal-only restricted parking). - $100 per calendar year 6. Non-Resident Golf Cart Decal/Placard - Placards can be used at designated metered parking, located between 21st Avenue North and 6th Avenue South, and at metered street ends, from 69th to 77th Avenues North (not to be used in decal-only restricted parking). - $100 per calendar year Again, please see the City of Myrtle Beach's Parking Meter webpage for the full explanation of each option and the requirements that need to be met to receive it: https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/.../parking.../index.php . City of Myrtle Beach P.O. Box 2468 Myrtle Beach, SC 29578 info@cityofmyrtlebeach.com Powered By Revize Login × Share this page Copy and past this code into your website. <a href="http://cms5.revize.com/revize/troymi/">Your Link Name</a> Share this page on your favorite Social network Facebook Twitter Google Plus Reddit Close 
