+subsequently amended.  In addition, a proposed heliport/helipad must comply with 14 
+CFR Part 157 – Notice of Construction, Alteration, Activation, and Deactivation of 
+ARTICLE III                                                          DEFINITIONS 
+  
+3-4 
+Airports, NFPA 418 Standard for Heliports, and the South Carolina Airports Act. 
+(Amended Ord. 2016-37) 
+ 
+ 306.9  Helistop.  A heliport without facilities appurtenant such as, but not limited to, parking, 
+  waiting room, fueling facilities or maintenance equipment. (Amended Ord. 2016-37) 
+ 
+ 306.10 Commercial Helicopter Operation.  An operation utilizing rotary-winged aircraft  
+  services or transportation, regardless of intent, wherin that operation receives  
+  something of value, including but not limited to financial compensation, in exchange 
