-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Side by side</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">The towns, with prices and rules</h2>
-<div style="overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy);min-width:680px"><thead><tr><th style="${S.th}">Area</th><th style="${S.th}">Price range</th><th style="${S.th}">Governed by</th><th style="${S.th}">What it is known for</th></tr></thead><tbody>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/little-river/', 'Little River')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$150,000 to $800,000</td><td style="${S.td}">Unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">Intracoastal Waterway marinas and fishing docks</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">Longs, inland</td><td style="${S.td}">Typically below the beach towns</td><td style="${S.td}">Unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">Acreage, affordable and rural</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/', 'North Myrtle Beach')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$300,000 to $2,500,000+</td><td style="${S.td}">City</td><td style="${S.td}">Wide beaches, beach houses and Ocean Drive</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/myrtle-beach/', 'Myrtle Beach')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$150,000 to $1,500,000+</td><td style="${S.td}">City</td><td style="${S.td}">The boardwalk, the most shops and restaurants</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/carolina-forest/', 'Carolina Forest')}</td><td style="${S.td}">Mostly newer construction</td><td style="${S.td}">Unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">The newest construction, master-planned</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/conway/', 'Conway')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$120,000 to $500,000</td><td style="${S.td}">City</td><td style="${S.td}">A historic downtown on the Waccamaw River</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/surfside-beach/', 'Surfside Beach')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$250,000 to $1,500,000</td><td style="${S.td}">Town</td><td style="${S.td}">A fishing pier and a small-town beach grid</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/garden-city/', 'Garden City')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$225,000 to $1,200,000</td><td style="${S.td}">Mostly unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">A peninsula between the ocean and the salt marsh</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/murrells-inlet/', 'Murrells Inlet')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$200,000 to $1,000,000+</td><td style="${S.td}">Unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">The MarshWalk restaurants on the saltwater creek</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/pawleys-island/', 'Pawleys Island')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$450,000 to $5,000,000+</td><td style="${S.td}">Town, plus unincorporated mainland</td><td style="${S.td}">Historic beach cottages, expensive, creek on one side, ocean on the other</td></tr>
-</tbody></table></div>
-<p style="${S.small};margin-top:.9rem">Price ranges are the working ranges on each area page and move with the market. Longs has no area page yet; prices there vary widely with land. Our page on the ${A('/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/', 'most affordable places to buy a home near Myrtle Beach')} compares Longs with Loris, Aynor, Conway and Georgetown. If you plan to rent the home out, the town ordinance and the HOA covenants for the address govern, and we will pull both. The feature column is what each area is physically known for, not a judgement about it. The town of Pawleys Island is entirely in Georgetown County. A Murrells Inlet mailing address can be in Horry County or in Georgetown County, which changes which county rules apply. The rules on the sand itself, dogs, tents and parking, differ by town as well, on our ${A('/buyers/relocating/beaches/', 'beach rules page')}. For the hospital nearest any address, see the ${A('/buyers/relocating/healthcare/', 'healthcare page')}.</p>
-<div style="${S.ctaBox}"><p style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600">Not sure which of these your budget reaches?</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#lead-form">Shortlist my towns</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div></section>
